<title>FRANCE: Fashion house Chanel buys beachwear firm Eres.</title>
<headline>Fashion house Chanel buys beachwear firm Eres.</headline>
<dateline>PARIS 1997-06-12</dateline>
<text>
<p>French fashion house Chanel has bought control of upmarket beachwear manufacturer Eres, a spokeswoman for Chanel said on Thursday.</p>
<p>Eres is a family-run business that generates 60 million francs ($10.3 million) in annual sales, roughly two-thirds of that in France and the rest abroad.</p>
<p>The companies declined to give the purchase price.</p>
<p>Chanel, owned by the Wertheimer brothers, was founded by designer Coco Chanel before World War Two and produces designer clothing, signature accessories and the world's best selling perfume, Chanel No 5. ($ = 5.821 French Francs)</p>
